 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S442-007\", \"clauses\": {\"solve_problems\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"One group has {a_phrase} and another group has {b_phrase}. If you put them together, how many items are there in all?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 is a two-group word problem that asks for the total, which is solving a problem. Its a_phrase and b_phrase come from F09 and F10, which print a count followed by items; that text is fine. The clause is producible.\"}, \"pictures\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F15\", \"template\": \"{group_a_str} — There {v} {a} {name_a}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F15 nests the picture families F12, F13, F20 and F22 in group_a_str, so a learner can solve from pictures. F15 itself is at fault (see failing_families), but the clause is producible.\"}, \"addition\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F24\", \"template\": \"Show {a} + {b} on the number line.\", \"reasoning\": \"F24 states the addition of a and b, using the cumulative vocabulary terms number line and the operation addition is named in the lc text. The clause is producible.\"}, \"sum_up_to_100\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F23\", \"template\": \"The two parts are {p1} and {p2}. What is the {word}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F23 asks for the sum of two parts drawn from the a and b domains. declared_bounds max_sum [0, 100] limits the sum to 100, and the word slot always prints sum. The clause is producible.\"}, \"without_regrouping\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F04\", \"template\": \"Add the ones: {ones_a} + {ones_b} = {ones_sum}. Keep {ones_sum} in the ones place.\", \"reasoning\": \"F04 adds the ones digits and keeps the sum in the ones place, which shows no carry. declared_bounds sets regrouping to false, and F01 prints nothing for the regrouping gate. The clause is producible.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F12\", \"F13\", \"F14\", \"F15\", \"F16\", \"F25\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"(Large group of {a} {pluralize})\", \"(Large group of {b} {pluralize})\", \"How many total {name_plural} are there?\", \"{group_a_str} — There {v} {a} {name_a}.\", \"{group_b_str} — {b} more {name_b} {v} added.\", \"The dot is at {a} and it moves forward {b} {num_word}. Starting from {a}, just count up {b} {num_word}. Which number will the dot land on?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"The noun slots in F12, F13, F14, F15 and F16 draw from the domain a noun from a fixed list, or its plural, with no link to the count, so the singular can print with any count (for example a count of 3 with the singular noun). In F15 and F16 the copula slot v is one of a fixed list, is or are, chosen independently of a or b, so the copula can disagree with the count. F12 and F13 print the count with the same unlinked noun. F15 and F16 also nest emoji pictograph families whose member choice is independent per slot and whose count has no declared link to a or b, and the noun named beside the picture has no declared link to the emoji shown, so the printed statement can be false about the picture. F25 chooses num_word from number and numbers with no link to b, so the dot sentence can read with the wrong number form for b. F06, F23, F24, F04 and the other families stay within the declared bounds and vocabulary.\"}",
